# L8 (QUALIFICATION): the strict ladder past 131k on EIGHT POOLED SEATS, on c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-full-audit (adapted from tp4-262k8-jobs L9b): eight prompts at 4096, 32768, 140000,
# 253920, 16384, 65536, 200000, 253000 tokens, 256 out; the matrix plan runs them CONCURRENT then each SOLO. Three seats are past 131k together (the 140k, 200k
# and 253k rungs, plus the 253,920 one: four). READ: concurrent byte-equal to solo for every user, rungs ~140k and ~253k included (strict policy); zero
# extent-audit mismatches; no refusal, no hang; Lever N chunking on the long arrivals shows no foreign route. Real time ~45.
# TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the ship/262k-full pack (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over that file on a throwaway
# commit of ship/262k-full (with its evidence files committed) and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Names no rig, card, host or registry. ORDER.txt has
# the order, stop rules, real minutes, NEEDS and the GO rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-10 is the ONE shipping image X0B builds: every job serves it.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-10
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-full-audit
C2_GATE_PLAN=matrix
C2_GATE_LENGTHS=4096,32768,140000,253920,16384,65536,200000,253000
C2_GATE_MAX_TOKENS=256
C2_GATE_JIT=record
C2_GATE_AUDITS=extent
